# .riskignore - suppresses Blueprint Visualizer risk findings
#
# Place this file next to the blueprint's root YAML. Every entry is a waiver:
# constitution Governance requires each one to be recorded in plan.md's
# Complexity Tracking table with the rule ID, the affected node, and the
# reason. Remove an entry as soon as the finding is fixed.
#
# Entries that match no finding produce a warning when the visualizer runs,
# so stale lines are reported rather than silently ignored.
#
# Three forms are accepted, one per line:
#   RULE-ID              every finding from that rule
#   RULE-ID:node_name    that rule, on the named node only
#   Exact finding title  any finding whose title matches exactly
#
# Prefer the narrowest form. The examples below are commented out so that
# copying this file suppresses nothing until you choose to.

# Rule on one node: the resolver node has no dependencies by design
# ND-001:target_resolver

# Exact title: a component that intentionally publishes no capabilities
# No capabilities or outputs defined

# Whole rule: avoid unless every finding from the rule is reviewed
# ND-005
